{
  "about": "Golden QR symbols and reference tables from two independent encoders, for test/qr.test.js. Made once by a scratch script outside the repository with python-qrcode 8.2 (every symbol: QRCode(version, error_correction, mask_pattern, border=0) over byte-mode data) and segno 1.6.6 (version and error-level choice with boost_error=True; the matrices of symbols with no pad codewords, because segno 1.6.6 inserts an extra 0x00 codeword before the pad codewords, which ISO/IEC 18004 7.4.10 does not; tables). Every symbol matched src/main/vendor/qrcodegen.js before it was written. inputs[]: the text (encoded as UTF-8 bytes in byte mode), the version and error level all three encoders choose for it at level M, encodeMask = the mask qr.encode picks on its own, padCodewords = pad codewords after the data. symbols[]: inputs[input] rendered with this mask (the encodeMask one, or forced in every encoder); bits uses the src/main/qr.js format: base64 of the size*size modules, row-major, MSB first, 1 = dark. Tables from segno: formatInfo[level][mask] (15 bits after the 0x5412 mask), versionInfo[version] (18 bits), alignment[version] (center coordinates), byteCapacityM[version - 1] (bytes at level M in byte mode), rs (Reed-Solomon ECC codewords for the data, computed from segno's GF(256) tables and generator polynomials), rsGeneratorExponents10 (the degree-10 generator: exponents of alpha after the leading 1).",
